.TH QFW_QISKIT_SIMPLE.SH 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Examples"
.SH NAME
qfw_qiskit_simple.sh \- submit one measured Qiskit circuit through QFw
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_qiskit_simple.sh [common-options] qubits
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw_qiskit_simple.sh
constructs a GHZ-style Qiskit circuit, measures every qubit, and submits it to
the selected QPM with 1,024 shots. The test prints measurement counts and a
statevector when the backend provides one.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I qubits
Positive circuit width.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --service-mode " mode"
Use application-owned
.B local
services or an existing
.B site
QPM. The default is local.
.TP
.BI --backend " name"
Select the QPM provider. The default is
.BR nwqsim .
.TP
.BI --site-config " path"
Override the activated site configuration.
.TP
.BI --runtime-config " path"
Override the installed runtime selected by the service mode.
.TP
.B --verbose
Enable shell tracing.
.PP
Common options must precede
.IR qubits .
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a four-qubit circuit on an application-owned NWQSim QPM:
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_qiskit_simple.sh --service-mode local --backend nwqsim 4
.EE
.PP
Run a two-qubit circuit on a site-owned IQM QPM:
.EX
cd "${QFW_SHARE_DIR}/examples"
\&./qfw_qiskit_simple.sh --service-mode site --backend iqm 2
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw_ghz.sh (1),
.BR qfw_run_all.sh (1),
.BR qfw-examples (7),
.BR qfw-srun (1),
.BR qfw-runtime.yaml (5)
